# Objects and props

Draw devices from real objects, then remove the detail that does not explain the action.

## Start from the real object

Look at a photo of the real device. Break it into simple shapes: circles, rectangles and parts of circles. Then keep only what the task needs.

A thermostat needs its dial and display, not its screws. A smart plug needs its button, not its vents.

## Keep objects flat

Draw objects from the front or the side, in flat colour. Show depth by layering one shape over another, not with a 3D view. A sensor in front of a wall is enough to show where it sits.

## Use real devices only

- Do not draw a manufacturer’s logo on a device.
- Do not invent a device that does not exist.

## Example

The [Characters example](illustration-characters.html#example) includes a thermostat with only its dial and display. Its screws, buttons and logo are removed.
